      "notes": [
        "In the protocol run, pad-40mb.jpg (41943040 B) returned 200 once (wall 4393ms) while pad-40mb-generated of identical size returned 503; on repeat 3/3 at 35 and 40 MiB fail, 3/3 at 25/30 MiB pass. Boundary is ~30-35 MiB and appears marginal/nondeterministic at the edge (128MB isolate memory).",
        "503 body is the Cloudflare \"Worker exceeded resource limits\" error page (error 1102 class), not a worker exception.",
        "Timer finding: on deployed workerd, performance.now() and Date.now() do NOT advance during synchronous CPU-bound JS (5e6-iteration busy loop -> delta 0 for both clocks) but DO advance across awaits (setTimeout(150) -> delta 150). Therefore init_ms/read_ms are 0 for all CPU-bound reads; cloud.jpg read_ms=255 reflects its awaited remote manifest fetch. Client wall_ms is the only reliable timing.",
        "Every deployed /read response showed cold=true on some requests and init_ms=0/read_ms=0; cold flag is per-isolate and requests scatter across isolates."
      ]
